From 59276a146ba68dc391fc50c7dd8b7b4411f40533 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kestrel <kestrel@invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 06:49:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add NameWindowsMemory: name Windows private memory's mappings
 by owner (default off)

Every NameWindowsMemory seconds a FEX-internal thread walks committed Windows
private memory and names its Linux mappings (PR_SET_VMA_ANON_NAME): win:heap
(Wine heaps: each heap, its subheaps and large blocks), win:stack (guard page),
win:exec (executable), win:gc (reservation of 16 GB or more), win:big (256 MB or
more), win:private. Ranges FEX named for itself are recorded and never
relabelled; a refused name no longer turns FEX's own naming off.
